# Gates: Security

Purpose:
  Security gate specifications for the SDDRA system.

Gate: SC

Must:
  Critical findings = 0
  High findings = 0
  Required controls = passed
  Security acceptance criteria = met

May:
  Medium findings with accepted risk (requires explicit decision)

Block:
  Critical findings
  unresolved High findings
  secret exposure
  authentication bypass
  payment double execution
  authorization bypass
  injection vulnerability
  insecure deserialization
  SSRF
  dependency with known exploit

GateCalculation:
  Gate status is calculated after all applicable controls run:

    PASS: no Critical/High findings, all required controls passed
    CONDITIONAL: Medium findings with accepted risk, all required controls passed
    FAIL: Critical or High findings unresolved, or required control failed

  PASS or CONDITIONAL allows chain to advance to VR.
  FAIL blocks chain and creates remediation task.

GateSpecifications:
  Individual gate specifications:

    SAST.sdd       — static application security testing
    DAST.sdd       — dynamic application security testing
    DEPENDENCY.sdd — dependency vulnerability scanning
    SECRETS.sdd    — secret detection
    API.sdd        — API security verification
    CONTAINER.sdd  — container security
    PENTEST.sdd    — penetration testing
    ABUSE.sdd      — abuse and load testing

  Each gate specification defines: AppliesTo, When, Tools, MustPass,
  MayPass, Block, OnFail, Exceptions.

Remediation:
  On FAIL:
    Finding created for each Critical/High issue
    Task created for each finding
    Chain returns to responsible stage
    After fix, SC re-evaluates

AcceptedRisk:
  Medium findings MAY be accepted as risk:
    Exception ID: EXC-003
    Finding: SEC-012
    Reason: Temporary compatibility requirement
    Owner: Security
    Expires: 2026-10-01
    Review: required

  Accepted risk MUST have an explicit exception record.
  Expired exceptions MUST be re-evaluated.
  Accepted risks are stored in @project/security/exceptions/.

